  "code": "foot_models/static_ik.py",
  "template": "each subject's OpenSimData/Mocap/IK/squats1_setup_ik.xml; the task set, weights, accuracy and constraint weight are identical in all 20 squat setups",
  "markers": "43 marker tasks applied. r_mknee, r_mankle, L_mknee and L_mankle are switched off: the static trials have them but the squat recordings do not, so the squats' inverse kinematics never used them",
  "reproduction_check": "the same code and settings rerun on each subject's squats1 markers reproduce the dataset's squats1 inverse kinematics: RMS marker error equal to within 0.002 mm, pelvis translations within 1.2 mm, centre of mass within 0.6 mm, leg and trunk coordinates within 3.2 degrees; forearm pronation, which the markers barely fix, differs by up to 18 degrees. The frame rule is sensitive to those sub-millimetre differences: the squats' frame counts change in 6 of 10 subjects (squat_ik_reproduction). The squats keep the dataset's own inverse kinematics."
 },
 "metrics": {
  "amendment_2": "VALIDATION_PLAN.md, amendment 2: forward-backward centre of pressure combined over both feet, along the model's forward axis, as a fraction of the mean foot length; per-foot forward values are not evaluated (the model puts each foot's under the centre of mass by convention); subjects without frames are reported as not evaluated",
  "amendment_3": "vertical force: the combined vertical force of both feet (the model's equals body weight by construction, so this tests only the body model's mass and the quasi-static assumption); per-foot vertical force is not evaluated. Each metric is also reported per subject for the static1 and the squat frames separately, descriptively; pass/fail stays on the pooled per-subject values",
